<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Upper Volta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1919–1984</span> · Also known as Haute-Volta, Republic of Upper Volta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volta-river">Volta</a> was a French colony in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> created in 1919 from parts of Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>, centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mossi">Mossi</a> kingdoms. It was divided among neighbouring colonies in 1932 and re-formed in 1947. It became independent in 1960 as the Republic of Upper Volta, which was renamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burkina-faso">Burkina Faso</a> in 1984.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/upper-volta.jpg" alt="Upper Volta" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: odder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Upper_Volta.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
